      "writtenOn": "2017-12-18T07:11:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem to be the case, I mean, at least there is no _internal_ padding:\n\nsizeof(struct ec_params_battery_dynamic_info)\u003d1\nsizeof(struct ec_response_battery_dynamic_info)\u003d16\nsizeof(struct ec_response_battery_static_info)\u003d40\nsizeof(struct ec_params_charger_control)\u003d5\n\nBut I think I see the issue, especially when using these structures on the master side, and I use some packed structures that definitely will not have the right alignment (padding to 32-bit would not help there, either, as there is a single byte crc8):\n\n       struct {\n               struct {\n                       struct ec_host_request4 head; \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c aligned\n                       struct ec_params_charger_control ctrl; \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c aligned\n                       uint8_t crc8;\n               } tx;\n               struct {\n                       struct ec_host_response4 head; \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c not aligned\n               } rx;\n       } __ec_align4 data;\n\nI will keep __ec_align4 in these structures, but rework the EC-EC master functions.",
